edEdge logic; edge weight is only set once from model.edges at graph build time via useMemo/useEdgesState.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Enable/disable switch on competency node does not change state\", \"actual\": \"Clicked the enabled/disabled Switch on the \\\"Agile Methodology\\\" node (trusted click, correct ref). Before and after: switch data-state stayed \\\"checked\\\", aria-checked stayed \\\"true\\\", node opacity stayed 1 (should become opacity-50/dimmed per source className logic when disabled), and the top summary panel's Coverage (69%) and Avg Level (3.4) values were unchanged, indicating the toggle produced no effect anywhere in the app.\", \"evidence\": \"onCheckedChange={() => onToggleEnabled(competency.id)} is wired in CompetencyNode.tsx and correctly updates model.competencies in CompetencyGraph.tsx's handleToggleEnabled, but the graph's React Flow nodes are created via useNodesState(initialNodes) where initialNodes is a useMemo — React Flow's useNodesState only consumes the initial value once and never re-syncs on subsequent re-renders, so the rendered node (and its data) never reflects the update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library panel lists 5 templates (Software Engineer [Current, Apply disabled], Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager), each showing category, competency count, connection count, and relevant tags, matching the expected browsing functionality.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template updates header/summary metrics but not the competency graph itself\", \"actual\": \"Clicked \\\"Apply\\\" on the \\\"Product Manager\\\" template. The page header correctly changed to \\\"Product Manager\\\" / \\\"Product\\\" / \\\"6 competencies\\\", and summary metrics updated (Coverage 78%, Avg Level 3.8, Critical Path 4: Product Strategy/User Research/Communication/